Subject: browser retint: skip quietly when the privileged half is not installed

Every theme switch printed three errors before this:

    omarchy-theme-set-browser: line 6:
      /home/…/.local/share/omarchy/install/helpers/browser-policy.sh:
      No such file or directory
    omarchy-theme-set-browser: line 12: browser_policy_theme_hex: command not found
    omarchy-theme-set-browser-policy: expected six lowercase hex digits, got ''

They are harmless -- nothing was written and the theme applied anyway -- but
they appear on every single theme change, and the obvious reading of them is
that a file is missing and ought to be restored. It should not be.

What the script does is tint the Chromium/Chrome/Edge/Brave window frame to
the theme colour, by writing a managed enterprise policy into

    /etc/chromium/policies/managed/color.json

That is a root-owned path, and upstream reaches it without a password prompt
because an Omarchy install puts two things in place that a checkout does not:
`/usr/bin/omarchy-theme-set-browser-policy`, and the sudoers rule in
`etc/sudoers.d/omarchy-theme-browser` that names exactly that path. This repo
installs neither -- it runs Omarchy from a checkout and adds no sudoers rules
-- and sudo on this box asks for a password.

So restoring the missing helper would not fix anything. It would replace a
harmless message with `sudo` asking for a password from inside a theme switch,
which runs as `bash -lc` out of the shell with no terminal to type into: a
theme change would stall or fail where it currently succeeds. The missing file
is the benign outcome; the noise is the only real problem.

This patch makes the script return before it sources anything when the helper
is absent, which is the same amount of work it does today and none of the
noise. Where the privileged half IS installed -- an ordinary Arch Omarchy --
the guard passes and the script behaves exactly as upstream wrote it, so this
is safe to carry across an update.

diff -u a/bin/omarchy-theme-set-browser b/bin/omarchy-theme-set-browser
--- a/bin/omarchy-theme-set-browser
+++ b/bin/omarchy-theme-set-browser
@@ -3,7 +3,14 @@
 # omarchy:summary=Apply the current theme color to Chromium, Chrome, Edge, and Brave
 # omarchy:hidden=true
 
-source "$OMARCHY_PATH/install/helpers/browser-policy.sh"
+# Kali: the privileged half of the browser retint is not installed on this
+# box, so there is nothing here to do. Returning before the helpers are
+# sourced is the whole change -- see the patch header for why reaching root
+# would be worse than skipping this.
+BROWSER_POLICY_HELPERS="$OMARCHY_PATH/install/helpers/browser-policy.sh"
+[[ -r $BROWSER_POLICY_HELPERS ]] || exit 0
+
+source "$BROWSER_POLICY_HELPERS"
 
 CHROMIUM_THEME=$HOME/.local/state/omarchy/current/theme/chromium.theme
 THEME_HEX_COLOR=$BROWSER_POLICY_DEFAULT_COLOR
